1
00:00:21,150 --> 00:00:22,390
(Episode 71)

2
00:00:30,590 --> 00:00:31,590
Father.

3
00:00:34,500 --> 00:00:37,730
Do you think it could be a memory instead of a dream?

4
00:00:38,600 --> 00:00:39,740
A memory?

5
00:00:39,740 --> 00:00:43,640
I'm not sure, but if the same scenes and situations...

6
00:00:43,640 --> 00:00:46,080
keep repeating in your dreams,

7
00:00:46,340 --> 00:00:50,180
maybe it's a subconscious memory appearing as a dream.

8
00:00:51,310 --> 00:00:52,820
The man in my dreams every night...

9
00:00:54,050 --> 00:00:55,180
The way he looked...

10
00:00:57,920 --> 00:00:58,960
Father...

11
00:00:59,890 --> 00:01:01,590
Was that your final moment?

12
00:01:35,960 --> 00:01:37,390
Why isn't she home yet?

13
00:01:51,170 --> 00:01:52,240
Hey.

14
00:01:53,140 --> 00:01:55,110
I don't think I'll make it home tonight.

15
00:01:55,380 --> 00:01:57,480
Don't wait up and sleep first, okay?. Okay.

16
00:02:01,180 --> 00:02:03,390
My gosh. It's already 1am.

17
00:02:04,420 --> 00:02:05,620
Are you really not going home tonight?

18
00:02:05,760 --> 00:02:08,590
What else can I do? My deadline is tomorrow morning.

19
00:02:09,830 --> 00:02:12,260
- What about you? - Same here, I guess.

20
00:02:12,260 --> 00:02:14,600
I might need to stay up all night to finish all these.

21
00:02:15,430 --> 00:02:16,870
Our meeting earlier was way too long.

22
00:02:16,930 --> 00:02:18,870
That's why I'm so behind on my work.

23
00:02:18,930 --> 00:02:20,070
Suit yourself.

24
00:02:32,250 --> 00:02:33,350
(Heart Mailbox)

25
00:02:33,420 --> 00:02:34,980
(Send Your Heart Here)

26
00:02:35,050 --> 00:02:37,250
(User 1234 Has Logged On)

27
00:02:37,520 --> 00:02:39,490
Did he have that dream again?

28
00:02:39,920 --> 00:02:41,490
Gosh, why is he still up at this hour?

29
00:02:43,790 --> 00:02:44,960
Still, it's a relief.

30
00:02:45,800 --> 00:02:48,460
At least he has somewhere like this to vent.

31
00:02:51,730 --> 00:02:53,340
(9 Jeongdam-ro 4-gil)

32
00:02:53,470 --> 00:02:54,470
What about Team Leader Ko?

33
00:02:54,600 --> 00:02:56,340
He went out early this morning. Said he had work.

34
00:02:56,610 --> 00:02:59,010
What? That early? What time?

35
00:02:59,710 --> 00:03:01,110
Around five, I think.

36
00:03:01,840 --> 00:03:04,350
I mean, the competition only ended a few days ago.

37
00:03:04,480 --> 00:03:05,720
Is he already that busy?

38
00:03:05,920 --> 00:03:09,650
I don't know. Our team hasn't even really started our meetings yet.

39
00:03:10,290 --> 00:03:12,690
I'll pack him a lunch later. You should take it to him.

40
00:03:13,020 --> 00:03:14,090
Okay, I will.

41
00:03:14,290 --> 00:03:17,190
Is Eun Nim skipping breakfast again today?

42
00:03:17,260 --> 00:03:19,900
Oh, right. Eun Nim didn't come home last night.

43
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:21,330
She said she's staying at the studio for work.

44
00:03:21,500 --> 00:03:25,570
What? Oh my. She'll ruin her health at this rate.

45
00:03:26,340 --> 00:03:28,470
I should pack a lunch for Eun Nim too.

46
00:03:28,670 --> 00:03:31,510
Hey, you know where Eun Nim's studio is, right?

47
00:03:31,910 --> 00:03:33,780
Yes. I'll text you the address.

48
00:03:43,220 --> 00:03:44,790
I'm sending this to Mom.

49
00:03:45,020 --> 00:03:48,220
I thought she'd be curious about what I had for breakfast.

50
00:03:48,290 --> 00:03:50,630
Bit Na, do you talk to your mom often?

51
00:03:50,790 --> 00:03:53,060
Yes. She sends me pictures sometimes too.

52
00:03:53,500 --> 00:03:56,800
Which country she's arrived in and what she ate.

53
00:03:57,400 --> 00:04:00,440
Oh, that's nice for you, Bit Na.

54
00:04:02,810 --> 00:04:04,470
- I should get going now. - Okay.

55
00:04:04,540 --> 00:04:06,880
- Bit Na, have a good day at school. - Okay, Dad.

56
00:04:10,550 --> 00:04:11,780
I hear loading and unloading packages...

57
00:04:11,850 --> 00:04:12,850
is exhausting work.

58
00:04:13,050 --> 00:04:15,890
What if he overworks himself and collapses?

59
00:04:16,450 --> 00:04:19,320
Is Daddy going to collapse, Grandma?

60
00:04:19,490 --> 00:04:21,890
What? No, no.

61
00:04:22,020 --> 00:04:25,190
Grandma was just saying that because she's worried about your dad.

62
00:04:26,260 --> 00:04:27,260
That's right, Bit Na.

63
00:04:27,330 --> 00:04:28,660
Grandma was just worrying over nothing.

64
00:04:28,800 --> 00:04:31,800
Your daddy won't collapse. Don't worry, okay?

65
00:04:31,870 --> 00:04:34,900
- I'm off to work, too. Eat, Bit Na. - Okay.

66
00:04:36,140 --> 00:04:37,770
It's okay. Go on and eat.

67
00:04:38,910 --> 00:04:41,380
(Gangsu Construction)

68
00:04:44,780 --> 00:04:46,620
What happened? Why did you come to work alone...

69
00:04:46,680 --> 00:04:47,680
without saying anything?

70
00:04:47,950 --> 00:04:50,150
I suddenly had an idea early this morning,

71
00:04:50,790 --> 00:04:52,820
so I wanted to strike while the iron was hot. Sorry.

72
00:04:53,420 --> 00:04:54,860
What kind of idea is it?

73
00:04:55,660 --> 00:04:57,190
I'll tell you when I've fleshed it out more.

74
00:04:57,690 --> 00:05:00,100
Oh, right. My mom packed you breakfast.

75
00:05:00,360 --> 00:05:02,200
We still have time, so let's eat together...

76
00:05:02,260 --> 00:05:03,270
in the break room.

77
00:05:03,400 --> 00:05:05,470
Your mother, honestly. I could've skipped a meal,

78
00:05:05,530 --> 00:05:06,900
but she went to all this trouble.

79
00:05:07,270 --> 00:05:10,710
- I'll eat it for lunch later. - No. When Hoppy speaks...

80
00:05:11,510 --> 00:05:13,740
Yes. Roary listens.

81
00:05:16,780 --> 00:05:19,950
- Hello, are you just getting in? - Yes.

82
00:05:32,390 --> 00:05:34,060
Pulling all-nighters is getting tough.

83
00:05:34,130 --> 00:05:35,560
I don't have the stamina anymore.

84
00:05:36,970 --> 00:05:39,030
Gosh, who takes this long to wash their face?

85
00:05:39,030 --> 00:05:41,940
- My gosh! - Writer.

86
00:05:42,770 --> 00:05:44,910
Writer, what's wrong?

87
00:05:50,580 --> 00:05:53,420
I turned on the water to wash my face, and the shower head...

88
00:05:55,150 --> 00:05:56,690
What do we do about this?

89
00:05:57,250 --> 00:06:01,320
First, take them off.

90
00:06:01,390 --> 00:06:02,760
What? Take them off?

91
00:06:03,190 --> 00:06:05,230
Gosh, we have to dry your clothes first.

92
00:06:05,290 --> 00:06:06,830
How can you go home like that?

93
00:06:08,600 --> 00:06:10,230
Here. Wear this.

94
00:06:11,000 --> 00:06:13,270
I'll take the clothes to a laundromat and get them dried.

95
00:06:13,340 --> 00:06:14,400
Give me your wet clothes.

96
00:06:25,450 --> 00:06:27,620
Okay, I'll leave them with you.

97
00:06:28,580 --> 00:06:29,590
Okay.

98
00:06:31,520 --> 00:06:32,620
Mom.

99
00:06:33,220 --> 00:06:34,690
Ma'am.

100
00:06:36,360 --> 00:06:38,130
Jo Eun Nim, why are you...

101
00:06:39,230 --> 00:06:43,470
- This is... - Hello? I'm a webtoon artist.

102
00:06:43,530 --> 00:06:47,100
- No. I'm Seo Seung Woo. - Who are you?

103
00:06:47,540 --> 00:06:49,440
What is going on here?

104
00:06:49,710 --> 00:06:52,070
What on earth did you do to my daughter?

105
00:06:52,310 --> 00:06:55,080
What? "Do?" I didn't do anything...

106
00:06:55,240 --> 00:06:58,680
Mom, it's not like that. The shower head just went off...

107
00:06:58,780 --> 00:07:01,850
- You jerk. - Wait a minute.

108
00:07:01,920 --> 00:07:03,520
You absolute scum. What is wrong with you?

109
00:07:03,590 --> 00:07:05,620
You punk. My daughter. What on earth happened?

110
00:07:05,690 --> 00:07:10,090
- No, that's not what happened. - That woman. Hey, you. Ma'am!

111
00:07:10,230 --> 00:07:13,530
Mom. What are you doing here?

112
00:07:13,730 --> 00:07:16,030
- You, get out of the way. Hey. - But...

113
00:07:16,100 --> 00:07:18,500
What do you think you're doing to someone's precious son?

114
00:07:18,630 --> 00:07:22,470
Well, perfect timing. Your son was practically...

115
00:07:22,540 --> 00:07:24,470
Mom, please. It's a misunderstanding.

116
00:07:24,540 --> 00:07:28,380
Yes. It's a misunderstanding. We are, really, truly innocent. Yes.

117
00:07:28,440 --> 00:07:30,410
What? Innocent? You call this innocent...

118
00:07:30,480 --> 00:07:31,910
when my child is half-naked?

119
00:07:31,980 --> 00:07:36,250
What kind of upbringing did you have? You...

120
00:07:36,320 --> 00:07:39,790
- You robber. - Robber?

121
00:07:40,360 --> 00:07:42,220
- Mom... - Are you quite finished?

122
00:07:42,490 --> 00:07:45,390
- You, get out of the way. Move. - Mom, calm down.

123
00:07:45,960 --> 00:07:48,000
- Move. - Calm down, please.

124
00:07:48,060 --> 00:07:50,530
Looking like some kind of gigolo.

125
00:07:50,600 --> 00:07:51,870
Hey. What are you going to do about this?

126
00:07:52,100 --> 00:07:53,770
What are you going to do, you punk? What are you going to do?

127
00:07:53,840 --> 00:07:55,700
What? A gigolo?

128
00:07:56,710 --> 00:07:58,810
- Get out of the way. Move. - My gosh.

129
00:07:59,170 --> 00:08:01,280
- You, move. Move. - Move. Move.

130
00:08:02,140 --> 00:08:04,410
Move. Or I'll...

131
00:08:06,450 --> 00:08:08,380
My goodness, Kang Yeon Ja.

132
00:08:09,890 --> 00:08:10,890
Yu Jung Ran.

133
00:08:17,490 --> 00:08:19,400
Gosh, that hurts.

134
00:08:20,430 --> 00:08:22,730
Why? Seriously, why are you doing this?

135
00:08:22,730 --> 00:08:25,030
It's not like we did anything.

136
00:08:25,900 --> 00:08:28,100
Is your back the neighbourhood's punching bag?

137
00:08:28,100 --> 00:08:29,540
Why do you always get beat up by random people?

138
00:08:29,610 --> 00:08:31,270
- Seriously. - Why?

139
00:08:31,710 --> 00:08:34,910
Wait, are you mad because Writer Jo's mother hit my back...

140
00:08:34,980 --> 00:08:36,780
when you're hitting my back right now too?

141
00:08:36,880 --> 00:08:40,120
That's right. Nobody lays a hand on your back but me.

142
00:08:40,180 --> 00:08:41,180
- Unbelievable. - Nobody.

143
00:08:41,250 --> 00:08:42,990
Mom, please, just...

144
00:08:44,750 --> 00:08:47,920
I know your menopause symptoms have gotten worse.

145
00:08:48,520 --> 00:08:49,890
But still, this is too much.

146
00:08:49,960 --> 00:08:52,930
How can you take out your stress by hitting your own son?

147
00:08:54,560 --> 00:08:55,630
From now on,

148
00:08:55,960 --> 00:08:57,900
you're banned from the studio. Got it?

149
00:08:58,200 --> 00:08:59,230
What?

150
00:08:59,800 --> 00:09:01,270
We're working on a project together.

151
00:09:01,340 --> 00:09:03,540
If I can't go to the studio, what am I supposed to do?

152
00:09:04,310 --> 00:09:05,540
That's not my problem.

153
00:09:06,080 --> 00:09:08,810
Don't spend a single second with her, you hear me?

154
00:09:09,450 --> 00:09:12,980
But you two are friends, right? And our fathers are all friends too.

155
00:09:13,580 --> 00:09:15,480
We cleared up all the misunderstandings right there,

156
00:09:15,550 --> 00:09:19,250
so why are you still acting like this? Why?

157
00:09:19,860 --> 00:09:20,920
I just pretended it was resolved.

158
00:09:21,460 --> 00:09:22,790
If her daughter is so important, she should know...

159
00:09:22,860 --> 00:09:24,030
other people's children are important too.

160
00:09:24,760 --> 00:09:26,200
So what if she's the Madam's daughter?

161
00:09:26,860 --> 00:09:28,560
This is just ridiculous.

162
00:09:31,030 --> 00:09:32,230
I told you not to let people hit you.

163
00:09:32,300 --> 00:09:33,600
Why do you let other people hit you? Why?

164
00:09:33,670 --> 00:09:34,670
I get it.

165
00:09:39,840 --> 00:09:42,440
You, don't go to that studio from now on.

166
00:09:42,810 --> 00:09:43,980
Mom, why are you being like this now?

167
00:09:44,250 --> 00:09:45,250
I explained everything.

168
00:09:45,310 --> 00:09:46,780
We've cleared up the misunderstanding.

169
00:09:46,950 --> 00:09:50,550
If I say don't go, then don't go. The two of you, in that tiny room,

170
00:09:50,620 --> 00:09:52,390
pulling all-nighters this whole time.

171
00:09:52,790 --> 00:09:54,260
My goodness, and I had no idea.

172
00:09:54,320 --> 00:09:57,960
- I was working. Working. - Be quiet. Go upstairs right now.

173
00:09:58,690 --> 00:10:02,130
- Banned from the studio, got it? - Mom.

174
00:10:02,200 --> 00:10:05,900
Go upstairs right now. I have to go pick up Bit Na,

175
00:10:06,270 --> 00:10:08,600
so don't you dare go to the studio. You'll be in big trouble.

176
00:10:12,440 --> 00:10:14,410
Where did this even come from?

177
00:10:15,640 --> 00:10:17,850
What did we even do?

178
00:10:20,380 --> 00:10:22,080
I'm going to go get Bit Na, Grandma.

179
00:10:22,990 --> 00:10:24,720
Did Yeon Ja ask you to?

180
00:10:25,420 --> 00:10:28,720
- No, I was just going to go. - Then sit down.

181
00:10:29,220 --> 00:10:33,330
You only do that if you're asked, or when we go to line dance.

182
00:10:33,460 --> 00:10:35,460
Aren't you overdoing it?

183
00:10:36,170 --> 00:10:37,370
Oh, I'm not overdoing anything.

184
00:10:37,830 --> 00:10:39,700
It's not like this is the first time I've gone to pick up Bit Na.

185
00:10:39,770 --> 00:10:43,340
A rumour will start at the preschool that you're Bit Na's mom.

186
00:10:43,410 --> 00:10:45,240
That'll ruin your marriage prospects.

187
00:10:45,310 --> 00:10:48,540
Oh, Grandma. I've never heard such a thing.

188
00:10:48,780 --> 00:10:53,520
If Eun Ae knows any decent guys, ask her to set you up.

189
00:10:53,980 --> 00:10:55,480
Seeing my granddaughter marry a man...

190
00:10:55,550 --> 00:10:57,250
with a respectable job at a big company...

191
00:10:57,890 --> 00:11:00,160
Oh, that's this old grandma's last wish.

192
00:11:00,220 --> 00:11:01,220
Not this again.

193
00:11:01,520 --> 00:11:03,790
Grandma, I'm into Natural Encounters.

194
00:11:04,060 --> 00:11:06,400
Natural Encounter? What's that now?

195
00:11:06,600 --> 00:11:08,900
It means I'm looking for a natural encounter.

196
00:11:08,900 --> 00:11:11,370
I hate blind dates and setups.

197
00:11:12,330 --> 00:11:14,670
Naturally and by chance,

198
00:11:15,140 --> 00:11:17,640
the right person I'm drawn to will just appear,

199
00:11:17,710 --> 00:11:20,840
- so don't you worry. - Naturally and by chance?

200
00:11:21,580 --> 00:11:23,610
You sure can talk.

201
00:11:23,680 --> 00:11:27,880
Cooped up in this tiny pancake shop day in and day out,

202
00:11:27,950 --> 00:11:30,590
when are you ever going to have a "Natural Encounter?" My goodness.

203
00:11:30,890 --> 00:11:34,690
- Daddy. - Oh, my Bit Na.

204
00:11:35,460 --> 00:11:37,690
- Have a good day at preschool? - Yes.

205
00:11:37,990 --> 00:11:40,100
Are you done now? Let's hurry inside.

206
00:11:40,160 --> 00:11:41,160
You need to eat before you go to work...

207
00:11:41,230 --> 00:11:43,100
- at the academy. - I don't have time to eat.

208
00:11:43,400 --> 00:11:45,570
I have to change, wash up, and leave right away.

209
00:11:45,630 --> 00:11:49,710
Even so. Come on, you have to eat to be able to work.

210
00:11:49,840 --> 00:11:50,840
I can just grab a roll of kimbap...

211
00:11:50,910 --> 00:11:52,210
from the snack shop in front of the academy.

212
00:11:52,940 --> 00:11:55,080
- Bit Na, shall we go in? - Okay, Daddy.

213
00:11:55,840 --> 00:11:58,650
- Daddy, blood. - Blood?

214
00:11:59,380 --> 00:12:01,350
- Eun Hyung. - Oh my.

215
00:12:02,080 --> 00:12:04,090
I haven't slept well recently...

216
00:12:04,150 --> 00:12:05,850
because I'm working on the summer break textbooks.

217
00:12:06,320 --> 00:12:07,790
Bit Na, don't worry. Daddy's okay.

218
00:12:09,190 --> 00:12:10,190
Blood?

219
00:12:10,760 --> 00:12:11,760
Eun Hyung...

220
00:12:12,130 --> 00:12:13,260
Oh, my.

221
00:12:15,760 --> 00:12:16,770
There she goes again.

222
00:12:17,800 --> 00:12:20,540
Thanks, Cho Rong. Bit Na, let's go inside. Come on.

223
00:12:20,840 --> 00:12:22,070
This is so upsetting.

224
00:12:25,010 --> 00:12:26,780
Oh no, what's going to happen to him?

225
00:12:26,880 --> 00:12:29,810
Stop meddling and get in here. Go trim the bean sprouts.

226
00:12:34,520 --> 00:12:36,350
(President Ko Dae Chi)

227
00:12:36,490 --> 00:12:37,490
You jerk.

228
00:12:37,920 --> 00:12:40,190
What? Did you just grab my collar?

229
00:12:40,460 --> 00:12:43,660
Hey, Secretary Jo, take a picture. Get this on video, quick.

230
00:12:43,990 --> 00:12:47,560
I'm not letting this slide. Hurry and get the shot.

231
00:12:48,060 --> 00:12:49,160
Seo Gwon Sik, what do you think you're doing?

232
00:12:49,700 --> 00:12:50,700
Stop it.

233
00:12:54,940 --> 00:12:56,770
That jerk...

234
00:12:57,340 --> 00:12:58,870
He was shooting daggers from his eyes.

235
00:13:00,180 --> 00:13:02,080
Is he still holding a grudge against me?

236
00:13:03,880 --> 00:13:05,050
Fat chance, you punk.

237
00:13:05,650 --> 00:13:06,880
The moment I'm made chairman,

238
00:13:06,950 --> 00:13:09,550
you're out of Gangsu Group for good. Out.

239
00:13:11,620 --> 00:13:12,620
Yes.

240
00:13:12,720 --> 00:13:14,620
(Gangsu Construction)

241
00:13:14,720 --> 00:13:16,930
The nerve of that jerk, coming in here...

242
00:13:16,990 --> 00:13:18,030
Just barging into the President's office...

243
00:13:18,090 --> 00:13:19,090
without a second thought.

244
00:13:19,430 --> 00:13:22,230
President Ko. I can't go down for this alone.

245
00:13:23,030 --> 00:13:24,830
I'm supposed to return to work next Monday,

246
00:13:25,370 --> 00:13:27,200
and if you don't block the disciplinary hearing by then,

247
00:13:28,370 --> 00:13:30,040
I'll have no choice but to blow the whistle.

248
00:13:31,640 --> 00:13:33,280
What? Blow the whistle?

249
00:13:34,140 --> 00:13:36,180
Then you won't get off scot-free either.

250
00:13:37,210 --> 00:13:39,110
You ordered me to steal information...

251
00:13:39,180 --> 00:13:41,280
from Team Two, using a promotion as bait,

252
00:13:41,550 --> 00:13:43,190
and to sabotage the elevator...

253
00:13:43,690 --> 00:13:44,690
and the CCTV footage...

254
00:13:45,050 --> 00:13:46,320
You were the one who told me to release it...

255
00:13:46,390 --> 00:13:47,660
at the presentation, weren't you?

256
00:13:48,190 --> 00:13:49,220
Enough, enough.

257
00:13:50,330 --> 00:13:52,060
Gosh. Hey.

258
00:13:52,860 --> 00:13:56,060
Broadcasting the video was your idea in the first place.

259
00:13:56,570 --> 00:13:59,770
Besides, I didn't even know Team Leader Ko had a panic disorder.

260
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:00,940
Regardless.

261
00:14:01,670 --> 00:14:03,140
As it stands, it looks like I'm going to be...

262
00:14:03,210 --> 00:14:04,470
the only one taking the fall for this.

263
00:14:06,410 --> 00:14:07,610
You need to take responsibility.

264
00:14:07,940 --> 00:14:09,510
Now, listen carefully. If you were really...

265
00:14:09,580 --> 00:14:11,280
being referred to the disciplinary committee,

266
00:14:11,350 --> 00:14:13,050
it would've happened the very next day.

267
00:14:13,120 --> 00:14:16,050
But it's been quiet, hasn't it? What do you think that means?

268
00:14:16,120 --> 00:14:18,050
It means they're dropping it, you idiot.

269
00:14:20,260 --> 00:14:21,260
Do you really think so?

270
00:14:22,220 --> 00:14:24,390
This is why you never plan anything big...

271
00:14:24,760 --> 00:14:28,060
with an idiot.

272
00:14:28,160 --> 00:14:30,330
What are you talking about? Get out, you idiot. Now.

273
00:14:30,970 --> 00:14:33,600
President Ko, I'll be putting my trust in you, then.

274
00:14:34,970 --> 00:14:36,070
- Yes. - Right.

275
00:14:37,970 --> 00:14:38,970
General Director.

276
00:14:39,240 --> 00:14:40,880
Han Ji Hun, what are you doing here?

277
00:14:41,510 --> 00:14:43,380
Weren't you told to stay home on suspension?

278
00:14:44,350 --> 00:14:46,480
I'm sorry.

279
00:14:47,580 --> 00:14:50,350
I had something urgent to discuss with President Ko.

280
00:14:51,690 --> 00:14:53,020
I'll get going, then.

281
00:14:57,190 --> 00:14:59,130
Was he the employee who was on suspension?

282
00:14:59,690 --> 00:15:01,560
What is it?

283
00:15:02,630 --> 00:15:04,070
We've decided to drop the disciplinary hearing...

284
00:15:04,130 --> 00:15:05,130
for Han Ji Hun.

285
00:15:05,700 --> 00:15:06,800
Is that so?

286
00:15:07,270 --> 00:15:10,740
So Team Leader Ko and Intern Jo aren't making an issue of it?

287
00:15:11,010 --> 00:15:12,010
No.

288
00:15:12,310 --> 00:15:14,410
They were the ones who first suggested dropping it.

289
00:15:16,450 --> 00:15:17,550
Well, I guess...

290
00:15:17,980 --> 00:15:19,710
making a bigger fuss would only draw more attention...

291
00:15:19,780 --> 00:15:20,950
to Team Leader Ko's health issues.

292
00:15:21,020 --> 00:15:24,150
Right. That was a smart move on their part.

293
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:25,920
Father.

294
00:15:26,620 --> 00:15:28,590
Please, just stop now. Okay?

295
00:15:29,060 --> 00:15:31,930
What do you mean, stop? Who are you to tell me to stop?

296
00:15:32,560 --> 00:15:34,360
You're the one who talked a big game and lost...

297
00:15:34,430 --> 00:15:35,960
the second round of the competition to Gyeol.

298
00:15:36,160 --> 00:15:37,830
There's still the third round of the competition.

299
00:15:38,570 --> 00:15:39,900
I lost the second round because of Joy,

300
00:15:39,970 --> 00:15:41,500
but I'm truly confident about the third one.

301
00:15:41,770 --> 00:15:42,770
Just you wait and see.

302
00:15:45,640 --> 00:15:49,580
I'm going to lose my mind. This is total insubordination.

303
00:15:50,110 --> 00:15:51,710
My friends, those worthless employees,

304
00:15:51,780 --> 00:15:53,150
and even my own son. All of them.

305
00:15:55,050 --> 00:15:56,080
Unbelievable.

306
00:16:02,220 --> 00:16:04,390
Chief Seo, if you have time after work,

307
00:16:04,460 --> 00:16:06,060
want to grab a drink somewhere?

308
00:16:07,130 --> 00:16:08,130
What?

309
00:16:08,960 --> 00:16:10,330
Let's catch up. It's been a while.

310
00:16:10,630 --> 00:16:13,000
Plus, tomorrow is the weekend, so we won't have to rush.

311
00:16:13,440 --> 00:16:14,900
Yes, sure. Why not?

312
00:16:15,840 --> 00:16:17,570
(Strategic Planning Office)

313
00:16:17,710 --> 00:16:19,840
Oh, yes. Do you have an update?

314
00:16:22,280 --> 00:16:25,950
(Meeting Room)

315
00:16:30,250 --> 00:16:31,250
He's been arrested?

316
00:16:31,790 --> 00:16:32,990
Oh, I see.

317
00:16:34,660 --> 00:16:36,590
What? You need a witness statement?

318
00:16:36,790 --> 00:16:39,460
You said you reported it because you happened to overhear the call,

319
00:16:39,860 --> 00:16:42,200
but your number is in the call log.

320
00:16:42,630 --> 00:16:44,030
I realised it was a voice phishing scam,

321
00:16:44,100 --> 00:16:45,100
so I didn't engage.

322
00:16:45,530 --> 00:16:47,600
There was no further harm done, so I don't see why...

323
00:16:47,670 --> 00:16:49,070
you insist on a witness statement.

324
00:16:50,370 --> 00:16:53,410
Right. I have nothing further to state.

325
00:16:54,280 --> 00:16:55,280
Okay.

326
00:16:59,780 --> 00:17:01,480
Wait, was that the police?

327
00:17:03,020 --> 00:17:04,020
Oh, yes.

328
00:17:04,550 --> 00:17:05,750
They said he's been arrested.

329
00:17:05,820 --> 00:17:07,620
Oh, really? Well, that's what should've happened.

330
00:17:08,020 --> 00:17:11,460
But you're sure you have nothing to do with this, right?

331
00:17:12,030 --> 00:17:13,800
Are you going to make me repeat myself?

332
00:17:14,230 --> 00:17:15,230
Let's go. We're done here.

333
00:17:15,300 --> 00:17:18,300
Hey, wait. Sit down. I have something to tell you.

334
00:17:23,710 --> 00:17:27,140
What? Jo Eun Ae's mother is the Madam's daughter?

335
00:17:27,680 --> 00:17:29,210
It still doesn't feel real.

336
00:17:29,610 --> 00:17:31,550
I can't believe Jo Eun Ae is my cousin.

337
00:17:31,980 --> 00:17:35,820
Oh, so if Ms. Jo Eun Ae is cousins with you...

338
00:17:36,450 --> 00:17:38,290
Well, that means she's Team Leader Ko's cousin too.

339
00:17:41,290 --> 00:17:42,320
Don't tell me...

340
00:17:42,990 --> 00:17:44,730
Just because the two of them are cousins,

341
00:17:45,060 --> 00:17:46,730
you're not hoping for something, are you?

342
00:17:47,760 --> 00:17:51,670
As you know, Gyeol was adopted, and Jo Eun Ae's mother isn't...

343
00:17:51,730 --> 00:17:53,170
my grandfather's biological daughter.

344
00:17:54,740 --> 00:17:57,140
It won't affect their relationship at all.

345
00:17:58,010 --> 00:18:01,080
So don't get your hopes up, not even a little.

346
00:18:01,740 --> 00:18:03,910
It's not like that. Please don't misunderstand.

347
00:18:03,980 --> 00:18:07,220
Okay. Oh, and I don't know if you've heard,

348
00:18:07,280 --> 00:18:09,680
but we decided to hold a living funeral for my grandfather.

349
00:18:10,020 --> 00:18:11,990
What? A living funeral?

350
00:18:14,390 --> 00:18:16,490
What? You were being blackmailed over that?

351
00:18:16,830 --> 00:18:18,630
While I was trying to find Madam's daughter,

352
00:18:19,060 --> 00:18:20,200
I was looking for the owner...

353
00:18:20,260 --> 00:18:21,730
of the construction site cafeteria from back then.

354
00:18:22,730 --> 00:18:23,770
It turns out that guy...

355
00:18:24,400 --> 00:18:25,970
was a guy I knew from prison.

356
00:18:27,300 --> 00:18:29,740
He threatened to tell my family and everyone at work...

357
00:18:29,800 --> 00:18:32,770
that I'm an ex-convict... and started demanding money.

358
00:18:34,110 --> 00:18:35,580
So that's why you've been acting so strange.

359
00:18:36,580 --> 00:18:38,880
But didn't you say you took care of it?

360
00:18:39,580 --> 00:18:40,580
I did.

361
00:18:41,680 --> 00:18:43,820
Because the guy got arrested for another crime.

362
00:18:44,490 --> 00:18:45,990
Well, isn't that a blessing in disguise?

363
00:18:46,890 --> 00:18:49,120
I thought so too at first, and I was relieved,

364
00:18:49,460 --> 00:18:52,390
but I think my Seung Ri was the one who handled it.

365
00:18:52,730 --> 00:18:53,730
What?

366
00:18:54,130 --> 00:18:57,170
How could Manager Seo have handled that?

367
00:18:57,470 --> 00:18:59,630
I don't know the details of how it happened either.

368
00:19:01,270 --> 00:19:03,240
Just the fact that I'm an ex-convict...

369
00:19:04,210 --> 00:19:06,010
must have been a huge shock to her.

370
00:19:15,120 --> 00:19:17,790
Gwon Sik, take it easy. Slow down.

371
00:19:25,890 --> 00:19:27,500
- Hold on. - What?

372
00:19:27,560 --> 00:19:28,560
Let's take a break.

373
00:19:29,030 --> 00:19:30,030
What?

374
00:19:30,500 --> 00:19:33,130
We've only run three kilometres. Are you giving up this easily?

375
00:19:33,200 --> 00:19:35,440
Do you think someone who runs every day is the same...

376
00:19:35,500 --> 00:19:37,110
as someone who hasn't run in a while?

377
00:19:45,980 --> 00:19:47,250
The night air feels nice.

378
00:19:49,050 --> 00:19:52,920
It does. But what is this? Out of nowhere,

379
00:19:53,050 --> 00:19:55,060
you want to go jogging with me every night?

380
00:19:55,320 --> 00:19:58,190
I want to spend every moment with you, Team Leader Ko.

381
00:19:58,790 --> 00:19:59,890
Why? Don't you like it?

382
00:20:00,530 --> 00:20:02,360
Looks like you have...

383
00:20:02,730 --> 00:20:05,370
completely fallen for me. This could get complicated.

384
00:20:05,770 --> 00:20:09,870
After a light jog like this and a lukewarm shower,

385
00:20:10,210 --> 00:20:11,640
you'll sleep much better.

386
00:20:12,070 --> 00:20:13,240
It's my secret to a good night's sleep.

387
00:20:16,440 --> 00:20:17,950
By the way, about the dream...

388
00:20:18,680 --> 00:20:20,620
You were right, Eun Ae.

389
00:20:20,980 --> 00:20:22,520
What? What do you mean?

390
00:20:22,780 --> 00:20:23,890
It wasn't a dream.

391
00:20:24,590 --> 00:20:25,920
It was a memory.

392
00:20:28,360 --> 00:20:29,420
I see.

393
00:20:30,360 --> 00:20:32,260
It must have been a very painful memory,

394
00:20:32,590 --> 00:20:34,560
for it to appear as a nightmare like that.

395
00:20:35,530 --> 00:20:36,600
I have no idea why...

396
00:20:36,660 --> 00:20:38,900
I couldn't remember it all this time.

397
00:20:39,930 --> 00:20:41,970
The fact that I had completely forgotten about it.

398
00:20:42,600 --> 00:20:43,610
I just don't get it.

399
00:20:44,610 --> 00:20:46,210
I did a little research.

400
00:20:46,810 --> 00:20:50,280
When it's hard to cope with trauma or extreme stress,

401
00:20:50,610 --> 00:20:53,010
your memories can be temporarily erased...

402
00:20:53,080 --> 00:20:54,820
as a self-defence mechanism.

403
00:20:55,480 --> 00:20:58,790
It could be a form of selective amnesia.

404
00:20:59,020 --> 00:21:00,990
Selective amnesia?

405
00:21:02,220 --> 00:21:03,220
Then,

406
00:21:03,460 --> 00:21:06,800
there might be other memories I don't know about yet.

407
00:21:07,230 --> 00:21:08,930
Well, maybe...

408
00:21:09,730 --> 00:21:12,600
you should consider talking to a professional?

409
00:21:13,300 --> 00:21:15,100
Are you talking about seeing a psychiatrist?

410
00:21:15,940 --> 00:21:17,510
I don't think it's at that stage yet.

411
00:21:18,370 --> 00:21:20,780
Besides, I've already found my own way of coping.

412
00:21:21,410 --> 00:21:24,410
- A way of coping? - The Heart Mail app you made.

413
00:21:25,150 --> 00:21:27,720
There, I'm writing the letters to myself...

414
00:21:27,780 --> 00:21:29,350
that I could never send.

415
00:21:30,720 --> 00:21:32,020
That's wonderful, really.

416
00:21:33,720 --> 00:21:34,760
Thank you.

417
00:21:35,190 --> 00:21:37,760
For trusting me and starting to write.

418
00:21:38,260 --> 00:21:41,530
Don't worry. I may not look it, but I'm tough.

419
00:21:42,160 --> 00:21:45,870
What part of you is tough?

420
00:21:46,630 --> 00:21:48,740
Not physically tough. Emotionally tough.

421
00:21:48,940 --> 00:21:50,940
And besides, I'm actually pretty ripped.

422
00:21:51,010 --> 00:21:52,610
- Why are you being like this? - Want to touch them?

423
00:21:54,080 --> 00:21:56,080
So I'm telling you, don't worry.

424
00:21:58,010 --> 00:22:02,020
- Should we start running again? - What? Hey. Wait up. Seriously.

425
00:22:12,930 --> 00:22:14,200
Just...

426
00:22:15,100 --> 00:22:17,400
how much longer?

427
00:22:20,740 --> 00:22:22,300
Mother, what are you doing?

428
00:22:23,810 --> 00:22:25,270
I need to know how many people will be here that day.

429
00:22:25,670 --> 00:22:27,040
I'm just jotting down a rough estimate.

430
00:22:27,610 --> 00:22:30,650
I need to have an idea of how much food to prepare.

431
00:22:31,510 --> 00:22:33,780
Mother, about what Father said...

432
00:22:33,850 --> 00:22:36,480
Can we really treat it like a party?

433
00:22:36,920 --> 00:22:39,390
But a funeral is still a funeral.

434
00:22:39,820 --> 00:22:42,520
Then just think of it as a family celebration.

435
00:22:43,260 --> 00:22:45,890
- It's what your father wanted. - A celebration?

436
00:22:46,530 --> 00:22:48,260
A celebration is a party.

437
00:22:48,860 --> 00:22:51,530
Then I'll be the head director for the party.

438
00:22:52,070 --> 00:22:54,270
And this time, I'm skipping all the French-style desserts...

439
00:22:54,340 --> 00:22:56,440
- and whatnot. - Why's that?

440
00:22:57,370 --> 00:22:59,540
You were going on and on about France.

441
00:22:59,610 --> 00:23:02,180
I can't stand to see Kang Yeon Ja showing off again.

442
00:23:07,250 --> 00:23:10,420
I'll be counting on you from now on.

443
00:23:10,950 --> 00:23:11,950
Pardon?

444
00:23:12,390 --> 00:23:13,920
I know you may not be thrilled about it,

445
00:23:13,990 --> 00:23:15,460
but as things stand,

446
00:23:16,190 --> 00:23:19,490
I'm asking you to please get along with my daughter.

447
00:23:20,930 --> 00:23:23,800
There's nothing to "get along" about.

448
00:23:24,300 --> 00:23:26,400
As long as she isn't legally part of the family.

449
00:23:28,900 --> 00:23:31,510
But Mother, how did you recognise her?

450
00:23:31,970 --> 00:23:34,110
You didn't recognise each other at all at first.

451
00:23:34,710 --> 00:23:35,710
That's true.

452
00:23:36,380 --> 00:23:37,380
Back then...

453
00:23:37,710 --> 00:23:39,010
I can't believe I didn't recognise her...

454
00:23:39,080 --> 00:23:40,280
when she was right in front of me.

455
00:23:41,350 --> 00:23:43,620
Well, Dae Chi and I found out a long time ago,

456
00:23:43,690 --> 00:23:45,490
after we got the DNA test results...

457
00:23:45,550 --> 00:23:46,990
What are you talking about?

458
00:23:47,790 --> 00:23:49,060
A DNA test?

459
00:23:49,660 --> 00:23:50,730
You scared me.

460
00:23:51,630 --> 00:23:52,660
Wait, so...

461
00:23:53,360 --> 00:23:54,700
you and your husband...

462
00:23:55,160 --> 00:23:57,400
Are you saying you knew even before I did?

463
00:23:58,170 --> 00:23:59,170
Is that right?

464
00:24:00,870 --> 00:24:02,640
I'm sorry, Father, Mother.

465
00:24:09,880 --> 00:24:11,480
Heading to the driving range?

466
00:24:11,910 --> 00:24:15,050
I have a round next week, so I'm thinking of hitting a few balls.

467
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:19,290
- I'm not sure I'm doing this right. - Golf? Yes, it's a great workout.

468
00:24:21,320 --> 00:24:22,660
You know, lately...

469
00:24:23,060 --> 00:24:26,830
I've discovered the world of dance. What do you think?

470
00:24:27,330 --> 00:24:28,560
That's all fine, man, but...

471
00:24:29,000 --> 00:24:31,470
whether it's dancing or golf, with any sport,

472
00:24:31,530 --> 00:24:33,900
the key is just to relax.

473
00:24:34,070 --> 00:24:36,970
See? I'm not using any force at all.

474
00:24:37,410 --> 00:24:40,140
- Am I tense? I'm not. - Dae Chi!

475
00:24:43,510 --> 00:24:44,550
Father.

476
00:24:45,410 --> 00:24:46,550
Come to my room.

477
00:24:46,950 --> 00:24:49,950
Father, what's this all of a sudden?

478
00:24:50,850 --> 00:24:53,120
- You too. - What? Me too?

479
00:24:53,390 --> 00:24:56,120
Is something wrong, Chairman?

480
00:24:58,530 --> 00:24:59,560
Gosh, this looks bad.

481
00:25:01,800 --> 00:25:02,930
What's gotten into him?

482
00:25:03,260 --> 00:25:04,770
Let's just go in.

483
00:25:07,900 --> 00:25:11,740
He must've done something seriously wrong again.

484
00:25:11,740 --> 00:25:15,310
My gosh, Dae Chi.

485
00:25:16,440 --> 00:25:18,080
What were you thinking? Why?

486
00:25:18,980 --> 00:25:22,880
How could you get a DNA test and still hide it from us?

487
00:25:25,450 --> 00:25:26,550
I'm sorry, Father.

488
00:25:27,220 --> 00:25:28,220
Sorry?

489
00:25:28,590 --> 00:25:30,090
Do you think a simple "sorry" is enough?

490
00:25:31,060 --> 00:25:33,290
Your mother and I were searching so desperately for her.

491
00:25:34,030 --> 00:25:35,460
And you still call yourself my son?

492
00:25:37,130 --> 00:25:40,330
I have no excuses.

493
00:25:41,900 --> 00:25:43,640
Actually, I have a question for you, Father.

494
00:25:44,910 --> 00:25:46,910
Am I really your son?

495
00:25:47,380 --> 00:25:48,540
What?

496
00:25:49,080 --> 00:25:50,580
What am I in this family?

497
00:25:51,250 --> 00:25:52,380
To be blunt, Father, you treat me...

498
00:25:52,450 --> 00:25:54,880
worse than you treat Chief Seo or Gyeol.

499
00:25:55,520 --> 00:25:57,250
If you had just been open with me from the start,

500
00:25:58,120 --> 00:25:59,790
I wouldn't have done this.

501
00:26:00,420 --> 00:26:02,320
It's because you constantly push me away...

502
00:26:02,390 --> 00:26:05,990
Do you hear what you're saying? Is that your excuse?

503
00:26:07,060 --> 00:26:09,960
Father, it's all my fault,

504
00:26:10,160 --> 00:26:12,170
so please don't be too hard on him.

505
00:26:12,800 --> 00:26:14,400
I was the one who figured it out first,

506
00:26:14,670 --> 00:26:18,240
and I grabbed Kang Yeon Ja by the hair, so he just...

507
00:26:19,410 --> 00:26:21,440
You grabbed Yeon Soon by the hair?

508
00:26:23,850 --> 00:26:26,410
- When was this? - I mean...

509
00:26:26,680 --> 00:26:27,880
That was, let's see.

510
00:26:28,720 --> 00:26:29,980
One, two...

511
00:26:30,550 --> 00:26:31,620
It was...

512
00:26:32,120 --> 00:26:37,020
- shortly after Gyeol left home. - What?

513
00:26:37,960 --> 00:26:41,660
You mean you already knew it all back then?

514
00:26:44,900 --> 00:26:45,930
Listen carefully,

515
00:26:46,700 --> 00:26:47,840
both of you.

516
00:26:48,700 --> 00:26:51,770
I'm going to officially add Yeon Soon to our family.

517
00:26:54,140 --> 00:26:55,140
What?

518
00:26:55,810 --> 00:26:56,880
- Father. - Father.

519
00:27:18,270 --> 00:27:21,000
(Our Happy Days)

520
00:27:21,070 --> 00:27:24,610
I saw you opened the safe. You must have read the will.

521
00:27:24,670 --> 00:27:26,240
No, I didn't, Father.

522
00:27:26,310 --> 00:27:29,910
Can't I see you act mature for once before I die?

523
00:27:29,980 --> 00:27:32,550
Your biological father. When and how did he pass away?

524
00:27:32,610 --> 00:27:34,820
Don't ask him about it until he brings it up.

525
00:27:34,880 --> 00:27:36,280
No need to reopen old wounds.

526
00:27:36,380 --> 00:27:39,490
You were at my father's funeral twenty-five years ago, right?

527
00:27:39,550 --> 00:27:42,320
Oh, right. I went with the Chairman.

528
00:27:42,490 --> 00:27:44,030
But why the sudden question?

529
00:27:44,030 --> 00:27:45,830
- Right, Secretary Ju. - I can't believe this.

530
00:27:45,830 --> 00:27:47,360
Why didn't I think of that before?

531
00:27:52,730 --> 00:27:55,770
(Our Happy Days)
